CORE
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Two pointer-to-integer casts of the same element of a large (unbounded) pointer
array must see the same pointer.  The cast converted its operand outside the
cache, so the second conversion of arr[i] got fresh literals that no array
constraint ties to the first: a false alarm (port of upstream 115b2148ed).
